      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Appleby's first school, founded before 1900, became the first independent school district in Nacogdoches County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Appleby%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By World War I, Appleby boasted nearly 1,000 residents and four churches, two gins, four sawmills, two hotels, and several drugstores.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Appleby%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Before settlers arrived in the 1820s, the site that is now Appleby was a Caddo Indian village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Appleby%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
